A 	erm{norm} on a vector space $V$ over $\R$ is a function $
orm{\cdot} : V 	o \R$ with
$
orm{x} \ge 0$, $
orm{\lambda x} = |\lambda| \, 
orm{x}$ and
$
orm{x + y} \le 
orm{x} + 
orm{y}$; macros defined in the text work in its formulas too.
\greet{reader} \greet[dear]{patient reader}
\[ 
orm{\sum_{i=1}^n x_i} \le \sum_{i=1}^n 
orm{x_i}. \]
